    <string name="book_help_text">Setting up\n\n• Put the phone on a tripod or overhead stand, looking straight down, parallel to the table.\n• Put a dark, matte cloth under the book. The page edges need to stand out for page detection and curve flattening.\n• Use two lights, one on each side at about 45 degrees. No light straight overhead (glare and shadows).\n• Optional: a sheet of glass or clear acrylic to press the pages flat. With glass on, set curve flattening to Off for that book.\n• Use a Bluetooth camera remote (it sends volume key presses), keep the phone on a charger, and turn on Do Not Disturb.\n\nScanning\n\n1. New book: enter the title, pick the language, say whether the book is printed with ʻokina and kahakō, and pick the layout.\n2. Setup shot: tap Detect page, drag the corners to the page edges and the dashed line onto the spine, rotate until the thumbnail is upright, then Confirm. The app locks focus, exposure and white balance and measures the page.\n3. Capture: the border is red while a page turns, yellow while things settle, and green when ready. Press the remote, a volume key, or the Capture button. Turn on Auto to shoot whenever the border stays green.\n4. Processing runs in the background. Each shot is cropped, split at the spine, flattened, straightened and read with on-device OCR.\n5. Review: the grid shows a badge per page. Open Flags to fix uncertain words one at a time. Page number jumps are shown with a Reshoot button.\n6. Export: searchable PDF, Word, or both.\n\nTip: long-press the state label on the capture screen to tune thresholds.</string>
